WEBVTT


00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:56.846
Mom! Jethro's eating my underwear!


00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:03.182
Here, piggy, piggy, piggy. Jethro.


00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:06.187
Mom, before she starts,
there isn't a shred of evidence


00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:09.728
-to support her allegations.
-Gillian, your son is a psycho.


00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:14.562
-He booby-trapped my hair dryer.
-Nice hypothesis, but you can't prove it.


00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:19.397
-Yeah, but l can hurt you.
-Mom! Mom! She needs to be medicated.


00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.833
-Come on, Jethro.
-Come here.


00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.978
l hate this family. Come here.


00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:29.581
Jethro, you're getting a time out.


00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:45.155
Come on, guys. Backpack.


00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:54.062
-What? lt's in style.
-lt's inappropriate. Go put on some jeans.


00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.505
And spit out the gum.


00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.114
So, what color do you want to wear today?


00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:05.715
Red? Blue? Purple?


00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.917
Pink, Momma, pink.


00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:11.557
-Farren.
-What? You said jeans.


00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.618
l meant in your size.


00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:20.798
Come on, guys. Come on.
We don't want to be late. There you go.


00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.832
Come on, sweetie.


00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.143
-No!
-Get out!


00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.279
No fighting.


00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:49.956
Allow me.


00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.458
-Hi.
-Hi.


00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:54.431
-Are we still on for dinner?
-l'll be there.


00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.030
We have an audience.


00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:00.964
-Yuck. l'm going to vomit.
-He is such a loser.


00:04:01.074 --> 00:04:03.008
l like Bob. He's nice.


00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.169
He's a boring pen importer.
He does the same routine every day.


00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:09.146
-He's like a robot.
-That's 'cause he is a robot.


00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:14.118
A cyborg, sent from the future,
to destroy humanity. Starting with us.


00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:21.789
Well, it's been three months.
Happy anniversary.


00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.466
What is it?


00:04:32.939 --> 00:04:35.339
l have to tell you about my job.


00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.074
This might shock you,


00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:43.978
but you should know everything
before this relationship goes further.


00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.679
-Don't, Bob.
-What?


00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:51.188
l'm very happy when l'm with you.


00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:54.155
No one has ever made me laugh like you do,


00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.358
and if l were a single woman,
l could see a real future for us.


00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.431
But l'm a package deal.


00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:01.925
What do you mean?


00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:06.761
My kids are my priority and.. .
How can l put this gently?


00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.931
-They hate me.
-Yeah.


00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:13.374
-l can make them like me.
-See?


00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:16.846
You can't make kids like you,
not mine or anyone's.


00:05:19.185 --> 00:05:21.847
My kids have been through a lot, and.. .


00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:26.220
l don't think we should take the next step
until they warm up to you.


00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:29.054
Doesn't your happiness count?


00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:32.662
Excuse me.


00:05:36.636 --> 00:05:39.799
Sorry, l gotta go. Emergency at work.


00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:43.002
-No ink?
-lt's much bigger.


00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:46.739
Sorry, really.
l will explain everything tomorrow.


00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.240
Okay. l'll see you tomorrow.


00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:12.200
-What took you so long to get here?
-Six minutes.


00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:14.933
-You stop for a latte?
-l get it. You're.. .


00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:18.339
-What's the expression? Chopping my bust.
-Close enough.


00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:21.675
Poldark and a couple other Russkys
just went in the refinery.


00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:25.583
Then l was right. He's planning something.


00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.081
Maybe they just want to fill up
their gas tanks for free.


00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:30.417
-l couldn't blame them.
-No, that man's so crooked,


00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:32.923
he could eat nails and poop corkscrews.


00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:34.549
You're the world's foremost authority
on Poldark.


00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:35.991
What do you think he's up to?


00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:38.655
lf his mission is to sabotage
the world's oil reserves,


00:06:38.765 --> 00:06:41.825
why would he care about
some two-bit refinery like this one?


00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:45.133
l'll make sure you get a chance to ask him.


00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:02.853
How the heck are you going to get in there?
A jet pack?


00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:04.814
lt's in the shop.


00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:23.105
Wait for my signal.


00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:32.778
Yuri.


00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.983
-What's this?
-C-4.


00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:40.419
When we are done here, l want you
to blow this place to smithereens.


00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:21.060
Hurry up. l don't have all day.
There is no overtime here.


00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:45.417
Bob Ho.


00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:01.733
l would love to chat, but l gotta go.


00:09:49.388 --> 00:09:51.788
-Up there. Go, go, go, go.
-Move it.


00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:53.892
-Move.
-Hold it. Stay where you are.


00:09:54.026 --> 00:09:57.518
That was fun. A good aerobic workout.


00:09:59.398 --> 00:10:01.764
We should do this again sometime.


00:10:01.968 --> 00:10:03.663
Okay, Poldark, let's go.


00:10:04.537 --> 00:10:06.596
<i>We have suspect in custody.</i>


00:10:09.575 --> 00:10:12.476
Did you see the look
on Poldark's face, man?


00:10:14.981 --> 00:10:17.415
Brilliant work, Bob. Unbelievable.


00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.414
l really hate to see you go home.
You're the best agent l've ever had.


00:10:20.653 --> 00:10:23.053
Hey, you know l'm standing right here.


00:10:23.155 --> 00:10:26.022
Maybe l can get your government
to loan you to me just a little bit longer.


00:10:26.125 --> 00:10:29.959
No. This was my last assignment.
l'm retiring.


00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:36.034
-Don't tell me because of Gillian.
-l want a normal life. l want to get married.


00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:38.365
Oh, heck, man. Don't get married.


00:10:38.471 --> 00:10:40.666
Just find some woman
that you're going to hate in five years


00:10:40.773 --> 00:10:42.707
and give her your house.


00:10:43.809 --> 00:10:47.472
Keep the watch.
A memento, compliments of the ClA.


00:10:48.981 --> 00:10:51.415
So, Gillian? ls that the woman
that lives next door to your cover house?


00:10:51.517 --> 00:10:55.385
-Yeah, they've been stepping out.
-l could never give up this life for a woman.


00:10:55.554 --> 00:10:56.646
We're spies, man.


00:10:56.756 --> 00:10:59.384
Every little boy wants to be a spy.
lt's the life.


00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:02.120
All the hours you spend
sitting alone in a little room like this,


00:11:02.228 --> 00:11:04.526
eating cold take-out food
in the back of a surveillance van,


00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:06.154
getting shot at all the time,


00:11:06.265 --> 00:11:08.825
learning how to pee in a bottle
in a moving vehicle.


00:11:09.301 --> 00:11:13.135
-You're doing the right thing.
-Only problem is that her kids hate me.


00:11:15.074 --> 00:11:16.598
You the man.


00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:19.271
Really gonna miss you, Ho.
Good luck with those kids.


00:11:19.378 --> 00:11:22.939
l've brought down dictators.
How tough can three kids be?


00:11:25.117 --> 00:11:26.482
-Come on, Ringo, come on.
-Here, kitty, kitty, kitty.


00:11:26.585 --> 00:11:29.520
-Ringo!
-Don't worry. Come on. Come on.


00:11:29.622 --> 00:11:31.681
-Come on. Right here.
-Come on, Ringo.


00:11:31.824 --> 00:11:33.291
-Come on, Ringo.
-Ringo.


00:11:33.392 --> 00:11:34.620
Hi, kids.


00:11:39.799 --> 00:11:42.563
l'm sorry about running out last night.


00:11:42.868 --> 00:11:45.860
-lt's all right. lt's your job.
-No, it was rude.


00:11:45.971 --> 00:11:48.565
l promise it will never happen again.


00:11:49.108 --> 00:11:51.542
Mom, what about Ringo?


00:11:52.945 --> 00:11:57.075
We've tried everything, sweetheart.
He'll come down when he's ready.


00:11:58.384 --> 00:11:59.578
You want to see
what l've been working on?


00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:00.982
Sure.


00:12:02.688 --> 00:12:07.318
Ringo, Ringo! Come on, kitty.
lt's not that far.


00:12:07.626 --> 00:12:10.117
Please, please, please, Ringo.


00:12:17.503 --> 00:12:18.970
There you go.


00:12:34.019 --> 00:12:36.715
-So, what do you think?
-Well.. .


00:12:39.425 --> 00:12:40.858
lt's a work-in-progress.


00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:43.258
Sadly, l didn't have any time
to work on it today.


00:12:43.429 --> 00:12:45.693
Cat was on the roof,
satellite's broken again.


00:12:45.798 --> 00:12:48.961
l spent two hours on hold
trying to get a repairman out here,


00:12:49.101 --> 00:12:52.229
and l can't stop thinking about last night.


00:12:52.905 --> 00:12:55.703
So, are we okay?


00:12:57.243 --> 00:12:59.074
l understand.


00:12:59.178 --> 00:13:02.375
lf a man marries you,
he marries all four of you.


00:13:03.315 --> 00:13:06.409
Don't forget the pig, the cat and the turtle.


00:13:08.087 --> 00:13:10.851
So, do you really like it?


00:13:11.524 --> 00:13:13.424
lt frightens me.


00:13:14.093 --> 00:13:18.029
Sometimes l think l found
the last honest man left in the world.


00:13:28.174 --> 00:13:30.540
l brought you all cookies.


00:13:33.679 --> 00:13:36.341
-Yes?
-ls it true? You're going to marry Bob?


00:13:36.515 --> 00:13:39.575
-What? Whoa! Calm down.
-You can't do this, Gillian.


00:13:39.685 --> 00:13:41.209
You're, like, so far above him.


00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:44.255
What she means is he's boring. He's a geek.


00:13:44.356 --> 00:13:47.325
He's a very nice man
who treats me very well.


00:13:47.526 --> 00:13:51.223
-He's a pen importer.
-He's a cyborg.


00:13:52.865 --> 00:13:55.231
You all don't know him like l do.


00:13:55.334 --> 00:13:58.360
He's very passionate about the world
and about my art.


00:13:58.504 --> 00:14:01.905
He likes to talk about history,
science and politics.


00:14:02.775 --> 00:14:05.801
l see what you mean about
him not being boring.


00:14:08.514 --> 00:14:11.972
What you all call boring, l call dependable.


00:14:12.218 --> 00:14:15.415
For once, l'd like a man who goes to work
every day at the same time,


00:14:15.621 --> 00:14:17.646
and who comes home every single night.


00:14:17.823 --> 00:14:22.351
A man who doesn't lie, or cheat,
or leave his family the first time some.. .


00:14:32.972 --> 00:14:34.940
My happiness counts, too.


00:14:38.077 --> 00:14:40.409
l hate it when old people have feelings.


00:14:42.448 --> 00:14:44.313
We gotta deep-six Bob.


00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:01.228
-What's the story here?
-They hit Poldark's prison transport caravan


00:15:01.333 --> 00:15:04.166
-at the edge of town.
-Tell me he didn't get away.


00:15:04.536 --> 00:15:07.232
He's as gone as rum cake at an AA meeting.


00:15:07.339 --> 00:15:08.772
l'm telling you,
this whole thing was a setup.


00:15:08.874 --> 00:15:10.569
They knew he was coming.


00:15:12.444 --> 00:15:14.139
Are you saying
there's a mole in the agency?


00:15:14.246 --> 00:15:17.044
l'm not saying anything except he got away.


00:15:36.468 --> 00:15:37.901
Welcome back.


00:15:49.214 --> 00:15:53.446
Tatiana,
you can't imagine what it's like in there.


00:15:53.686 --> 00:15:58.453
The oppressive darkness and the torture
of empty days stretching for years.


00:15:59.091 --> 00:16:02.583
-Prison is hell.
-You were in there for four hours.


00:16:03.429 --> 00:16:05.294
Enough tearful reunion.


00:16:07.933 --> 00:16:11.334
l need a new batch of the formula
as soon as possible.


00:16:12.638 --> 00:16:15.106
We'll run another test in two days.


00:16:16.875 --> 00:16:20.675
l need a change of clothes.
Something current and fashionable.


00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:24.311
And something to eat
that does not come with a toy.


00:17:00.185 --> 00:17:03.052
<i>The Sea Hag's made Olive into a zombie.</i>


00:17:26.879 --> 00:17:28.779
Honey, we're getting ready
to carve pumpkins downstairs.


00:17:28.881 --> 00:17:30.746
-You want to join us?
-Absolutely!


00:17:30.849 --> 00:17:34.012
'Cause l'm a loser and l have no life.


00:17:34.186 --> 00:17:37.519
Did l mention we're going
to toast the pumpkin seeds?


00:17:38.223 --> 00:17:41.215
Come on. l want you to join the family.


00:17:41.326 --> 00:17:43.191
And l want some privacy.


00:17:43.295 --> 00:17:45.456
-Don't get fresh with me.
-l'll use whatever tone of voice


00:17:45.564 --> 00:17:48.431
-l want to use with you.
-Farren, l want you downstairs.. .


00:17:48.534 --> 00:17:50.092
No, l'm not going to come downstairs
right now. Get out.


00:17:50.202 --> 00:17:52.295
Farren, this is my house.
You will listen to me.


00:17:52.404 --> 00:17:55.601
You don't own me. Get out.
l said, get out, Gillian. Get out!


00:17:55.707 --> 00:17:57.265
Downstairs in five minutes.


00:17:57.376 --> 00:18:00.470
l hate this house. l hate this family. Get out!


00:18:07.853 --> 00:18:09.218
<i>Me spinach!</i>


00:18:12.958 --> 00:18:15.552
No, she won't hear me. l'm on the roof.


00:18:16.195 --> 00:18:20.154
lt's like the only place
l can get any privacy in this loony bin.


00:18:20.866 --> 00:18:23.357
l can't let Gillian marry this guy.


00:18:24.236 --> 00:18:27.501
No, it's not that.
l mean, you're right, he is a total drone,


00:18:27.606 --> 00:18:29.665
but that's not the issue.


00:18:29.775 --> 00:18:31.675
What's going to happen
when my dad comes back?


00:18:33.045 --> 00:18:35.605
He won't just leave me here alone.
He'll be back.


00:18:35.714 --> 00:18:39.810
And if she's married, what happens then?
l don't know.


00:18:49.094 --> 00:18:51.585
Mom, lan's feeding Jethro bacon.


00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:54.628
-Okay, that's just wrong.
-Why is it wrong?


00:19:10.048 --> 00:19:13.814
-Ho, Bob Ho.
-Hey. So, how's it going with those kids?


00:19:14.086 --> 00:19:16.077
l'm taking Gillian and the children
on a picnic.


00:19:16.188 --> 00:19:18.122
l'm going to force those kids to like me.


00:19:18.223 --> 00:19:22.455
Force them? You know, you might as well
try scratching your ear with your elbow.


00:19:23.395 --> 00:19:26.023
Guess what? Poldark escaped.


00:19:29.768 --> 00:19:34.137
-No longer my problem.
<i>-Yeah, l know, but we recovered a file.</i>


00:19:34.339 --> 00:19:36.933
lt seems to be an entry portal to a website.


00:19:37.109 --> 00:19:40.101
<i>We can't crack it.</i>
<i>l thought maybe you could take a look at it.</i>


00:19:40.412 --> 00:19:44.109
Hey, if you can figure it out, great.
lf you can't, no harm, no foul.


00:19:45.717 --> 00:19:48.880
As a favor to you.
Send it to my home computer.


00:19:49.021 --> 00:19:50.511
<i>Already did.</i>


00:19:51.123 --> 00:19:56.151
While l'm thinking about it, they suspect
there may be a mole at the agency.


00:19:56.495 --> 00:19:58.622
-They suspect me?
<i>-No.</i>


00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:02.427
You know Glaze thinks
you're the sharpest barb on the wire.


00:20:02.734 --> 00:20:04.725
l have no idea what that means.


00:20:05.404 --> 00:20:07.429
Hey, listen, man, have fun on your picnic.


00:20:07.539 --> 00:20:11.066
Just shoot me back
when you check out that file. Thanks.


00:20:28.126 --> 00:20:31.562
Puzzle encryption.
Let's see what you've got.


00:20:46.912 --> 00:20:49.676
-ls it noon already?
-No. l have bad news.


00:20:52.484 --> 00:20:55.544
-My father is in the hospital.
-That's terrible.


00:20:56.121 --> 00:20:58.180
He plays senior softball
and he slid into third.


00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:01.282
-Now he's having his hip replaced.
-That's terrible.


00:21:01.393 --> 00:21:05.261
l have to leave the kids
and fly to Denver to take care of Dad.


00:21:06.198 --> 00:21:09.031
-That's great.
-What are you talking about?


00:21:09.201 --> 00:21:10.498
Let me watch the kids.


00:21:10.602 --> 00:21:13.833
lt would give us a chance
to get to know each other.


00:21:13.939 --> 00:21:18.399
No, Bob. You? Them? l don't know.


00:21:18.744 --> 00:21:21.907
My aunt's flying in from San Antonio.
She's very good with the kids.


00:21:22.014 --> 00:21:25.882
-She was in the military.
-Gillian, this could be just what we need.


00:21:26.051 --> 00:21:28.383
You really think you can handle
that kind of pressure?


00:21:28.754 --> 00:21:31.587
The driving, the schoolwork,
and then there's Halloween.


00:21:31.757 --> 00:21:34.225
Getting their costumes,
finishing decorating the house?


00:21:34.326 --> 00:21:37.386
No problem. Halloween is my favorite.


00:21:37.596 --> 00:21:40.861
You have nothing to worry about.
They will be perfectly safe with me.


00:21:42.401 --> 00:21:44.699
lt's not them l'm worried about.


00:21:46.872 --> 00:21:49.932
-You can't be serious.
-lsn't there any other option?


00:21:50.042 --> 00:21:52.033
Foster care? Juvenile hall?


00:21:53.545 --> 00:21:55.410
Okay. You'll be fine.


00:21:56.148 --> 00:21:57.843
Love you guys.


00:22:00.085 --> 00:22:03.384
-l'm going to miss you.
-Yeah, as proven by this total abandonment.


00:22:03.488 --> 00:22:07.049
You'll survive. l'll buy you something
from the hospital gift shop.


00:22:07.159 --> 00:22:08.717
-Bye.
-Bye. Love you.


00:22:08.827 --> 00:22:10.920
-See you later.
-Bye.


00:22:15.901 --> 00:22:18.529
So, is this exciting, or what?


00:22:21.540 --> 00:22:26.034
Well, l'll just pack a few things,
and we'll go to your house, okay?


00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:41.250
A Flowbee. l knew he cut his own hair.


00:22:41.426 --> 00:22:43.826
Nothing telling in his DVD collection.


00:22:43.929 --> 00:22:46.727
Standard action movies,
mainstream comedies,


00:22:46.832 --> 00:22:49.665
no sci-fi, and nothing above PG-13.


00:22:51.703 --> 00:22:54.194
Hey, his computer. Let's check it out.


00:22:54.306 --> 00:22:56.831
Good idea.
There's got to be some dirt on there.


00:23:00.912 --> 00:23:03.176
Fashion Armageddon.


00:23:03.281 --> 00:23:06.614
l haven't forgotten, Colton.
l will look at the file.


00:23:06.752 --> 00:23:10.210
But this is important. What is Halloween?


00:23:12.624 --> 00:23:15.855
Farren, do you realize what this is?


00:23:16.461 --> 00:23:19.794
lt's got you all worked up.
Let me guess, a Klingon dictionary?


00:23:19.898 --> 00:23:23.356
You have me confused
with an entirely different class of geek.


00:23:23.468 --> 00:23:24.935
Stockholm GBH.


00:23:25.036 --> 00:23:28.403
Grievous Bodily Harm, live in Stockholm.


00:23:28.607 --> 00:23:31.804
This is one of the rarest bootleg concerts
in the world.


00:23:31.943 --> 00:23:35.470
-Why does Bob have it?
-Who cares? l'm gonna download it.


00:23:37.582 --> 00:23:40.346
This is my ticket to Coolsville.


00:23:49.494 --> 00:23:51.894
