Bob Ho.


00:50:43.607 --> 00:50:49.443
He is very tricky. The best at what he does.
He won't be easy to find.


00:50:50.013 --> 00:50:51.139
-Ms. Creel.
-Not now.


00:50:51.248 --> 00:50:56.015
lmagine you are Chinese, highly trained,
and you want to disappear.


00:50:56.119 --> 00:50:59.020
l see him climbing with
a bunch of skulls on a rope.


00:50:59.122 --> 00:51:03.320
Okay, he's not Conan the Barbarian.
Good try, though.


00:51:03.427 --> 00:51:05.190
No, l see him. There.


00:51:10.667 --> 00:51:11.827
Go. Go!


00:51:15.272 --> 00:51:17.968
Don't kill him yet. We need information.


00:51:29.853 --> 00:51:33.687
Go, Bob, go! Go, Bob, go! Go, Bob, go!


00:51:34.191 --> 00:51:36.955
Come here, sweetheart. Get back here.


00:51:40.063 --> 00:51:41.621
Come here!


00:51:50.273 --> 00:51:51.433
Let go!


00:51:54.478 --> 00:51:57.038
-Get the bad lady, Bob.
-Let go!


00:51:57.914 --> 00:52:00.075
-Can you hold my turtle?
-Not now.


00:52:08.492 --> 00:52:10.119
Yay, Bob!


00:52:10.760 --> 00:52:11.920
That's it.


00:52:12.729 --> 00:52:13.787
You will pay for that,


00:52:13.897 --> 00:52:15.831
-little American princess.
-Bob, help!


00:52:32.649 --> 00:52:34.378
Again, again, again.


00:52:36.753 --> 00:52:37.720
Okay.


00:52:43.693 --> 00:52:46.821
-Why did you pull us out of school?
-Who cares? We're out.


00:52:46.963 --> 00:52:48.897
Why are you in the front seat anyway?
lt's my day.


00:52:48.999 --> 00:52:52.025
-No, it isn't. lt's my day.
-No, it's not your day. You're the liar.


00:52:52.135 --> 00:52:55.263
-No, today is my day.
-No, today is my day.


00:52:55.372 --> 00:52:57.863
-You're a liar.
-No. No. No.


00:52:57.974 --> 00:53:00.841
-All right, quiet!
-l'm still hungry.


00:53:09.519 --> 00:53:12.784
lt doesn't look like
they have chicken tenders here.


00:53:13.523 --> 00:53:15.991
Wait inside. l have to make a call.


00:53:24.201 --> 00:53:27.659
<i>-This is Firefly.</i>
-This is Bob Ho. l need help.


00:53:30.707 --> 00:53:33.039
Yeah, so l get pretty good grades
at this university.


00:53:33.143 --> 00:53:36.874
l'm top of the class.
l don't like to brag, but, you know.


00:53:36.980 --> 00:53:40.006
-Bob, this is Larry.
-Pleased to meet you, sir.


00:53:40.283 --> 00:53:42.808
-Let's get some food.
-He goes to the university.


00:53:42.919 --> 00:53:45.012
He's a poet. lsn't it cool?


00:53:48.258 --> 00:53:53.890
lt's rad. lt's awesome. lt's jiggy for shizzy.
lt's the bomb.


00:53:55.232 --> 00:53:57.291
-Let's go.
-Hey!


00:53:59.903 --> 00:54:01.495
How embarrassing.


00:54:01.871 --> 00:54:04.840
You know, most people don't like me
when they first meet me.


00:54:04.941 --> 00:54:06.340
But Larry did.


00:54:08.845 --> 00:54:12.406
l have two words for you, Larry. Thirteen.


00:54:29.866 --> 00:54:31.333
l have to go.


00:54:32.269 --> 00:54:37.263
All right, Nora. Come on.
You two stay at the table.


00:54:41.378 --> 00:54:42.367
No, no, no.


00:54:43.546 --> 00:54:45.275
l can't go in there.


00:54:56.293 --> 00:54:57.783
Boys are pigs.


00:55:02.399 --> 00:55:03.593
Careful.


00:55:13.977 --> 00:55:16.844
And the lion jumped on me,
and l killed him with my bare hands,


00:55:16.946 --> 00:55:18.641
and l saved the colonel's life.


00:55:18.748 --> 00:55:20.716
-You're brave.
-Thanks.


00:55:22.519 --> 00:55:26.717
How about this, Bob? The whole restaurant
and the waitress sat Larry here.


00:55:26.823 --> 00:55:29.792
-lsn't it great?
-lt's like it's fate or something.


00:55:29.926 --> 00:55:32.121
Really, sir, we're just goofing around.


00:55:32.228 --> 00:55:34.924
-Hey, Nora. Knock, knock.
-Who's there?


00:55:35.298 --> 00:55:37.698
-lrish stew.
-lrish stew who?


00:55:38.201 --> 00:55:40.431
lrish stew in the name of the law.


00:55:43.473 --> 00:55:46.738
Larry was telling me all about
the university. lt sounds great.


00:55:46.843 --> 00:55:49.812
-l'd be glad to give you a tour sometime.
-When pigs fly.


00:55:49.913 --> 00:55:51.744
lt's not up to you. You're not my dad.


00:55:51.848 --> 00:55:55.875
No, but l know that your mother
hasn't completely lost her mind.


00:55:55.985 --> 00:55:57.452
lt's just a tour, Bob.


00:55:57.554 --> 00:56:00.489
lt's not like he's asking me out on a date
or anything.


00:56:00.590 --> 00:56:01.784
Are you?


00:56:02.959 --> 00:56:05.189
No, it's just a friendly offer.


00:56:05.295 --> 00:56:08.458
Even if it was a date,
you still couldn't stop me.


00:56:13.636 --> 00:56:16.799
-What's your major, Larry?
-English Lit.


00:56:17.240 --> 00:56:19.401
Would you pass the soy sauce?


00:56:20.477 --> 00:56:23.378
That way l get a background in the classics.


00:56:28.685 --> 00:56:32.815
-You speak Russian, Larry?
-What's going on?


00:56:52.008 --> 00:56:55.910
-This is going to be painful.
-You're right about that.


00:56:59.682 --> 00:57:01.013
Go, go, go.


00:57:08.825 --> 00:57:11.123
Maybe you'll write a poem about this.


00:57:20.537 --> 00:57:22.004
Goodbye, Larry.


00:57:38.721 --> 00:57:40.018
Fine. He's too old for me.


00:57:40.123 --> 00:57:44.116
Bob, l don't want to be a princess anymore.
l want to be a cyborg.


00:57:45.061 --> 00:57:47.689
How did he find us so fast?
lt doesn't make sense.


00:57:47.797 --> 00:57:50.595
-Bob, what's going on?
-Please quiet, l'm trying to think.


00:57:50.700 --> 00:57:52.031
What do you mean, you're trying to think?


00:57:52.135 --> 00:57:54.968
-You just threw a man out the window.. .
-Who is he? What is.. .


00:57:55.071 --> 00:57:57.403
All right, all right, fine. Fine.


00:57:58.341 --> 00:58:03.142
l am international spy, on loan to the ClA
from the Chinese lntelligence Service.


00:58:03.246 --> 00:58:07.740
Someone wants me dead,
and ''Larry'' was a Russian operative, okay?


00:58:08.318 --> 00:58:10.047
Fine. Don't tell us.


00:58:11.821 --> 00:58:12.913
Cool.


00:58:18.328 --> 00:58:20.262
Why would he come alone?


00:58:21.898 --> 00:58:23.195
Stay here.


00:58:26.436 --> 00:58:28.461
-Where are the kids?
-lnside.


00:58:28.805 --> 00:58:31.603
Nothing else matters
until these kids are safe. Nothing.


00:58:31.708 --> 00:58:35.144
Of course. Colton set up that safe house
for them like you requested.


00:58:35.245 --> 00:58:38.806
-Hey, got that file on you?
-What file?


00:58:39.315 --> 00:58:42.045
The one Colton linked you to,
from Poldark's computer, your download.


00:58:42.151 --> 00:58:45.211
l didn't download it.
l never even got it open.


00:58:45.622 --> 00:58:48.648
Don't BS me, Bob. lt's classified material.
l need all copies.


00:58:48.758 --> 00:58:50.692
Why would you think l downloaded it?


00:58:50.827 --> 00:58:53.990
Unless someone told you l had,
someone who wanted it back.


00:58:54.097 --> 00:58:56.190
Let's not make this thing
harder than it has to be, Bob.


00:58:56.299 --> 00:58:57.960
Give me the file.


00:58:58.067 --> 00:59:00.627
You're a career officer. Why do this?


00:59:00.737 --> 00:59:03.433
l want out. Same as you.
We're both leaving for love.


00:59:03.540 --> 00:59:06.907
Only l love money
and Anton Poldark is match.com. The file.


00:59:09.979 --> 00:59:12.948
Wait. Take it easy.


00:59:19.923 --> 00:59:20.890
Good work.


00:59:21.324 --> 00:59:22.291
No.


00:59:27.196 --> 00:59:31.792
Can l just say, you are by far
the coolest guy my mom has ever dated.


00:59:33.670 --> 00:59:36.571
At least now l know how
that kid Larry found us so fast.


00:59:36.673 --> 00:59:38.231
-How?
-The watch.


00:59:38.841 --> 00:59:42.800
Glaze told me to keep the watch.
lt must have a tracking device.


00:59:43.880 --> 00:59:49.341
-Wow. You really are a spy.
-Gillian is totally going to freak.


01:00:11.407 --> 01:00:13.238
What are you doing?


01:00:13.509 --> 01:00:17.570
There's iron in these rocks.
lt will hide the signal. Watch, please.


01:00:18.348 --> 01:00:20.816
You realize if l told anyone at school
this story,


01:00:20.917 --> 01:00:23.681
l'd get detention for a year for lying.


01:00:30.994 --> 01:00:33.485
-Yes.
<i>-Hey, partner. Where're you at?</i>


01:00:35.198 --> 01:00:38.861
-Why do you ask?
-l needed to pick up that file l sent you.


01:00:38.968 --> 01:00:41.198
<i>You know,</i>
<i>the one l wanted you to open for me.</i>


01:00:44.741 --> 01:00:46.572
<i>Bob, you there?</i>


01:00:46.709 --> 01:00:49.872
Colton, l never thought
you would have sold out to Poldark.


01:00:49.979 --> 01:00:54.541
Hey, that's crazy, man. Something's wrong.
We need to get together and talk.


01:00:55.551 --> 01:00:59.248
-Nice try.
-Bob? Bob?


01:01:06.462 --> 01:01:11.365
-We'll be safe here. l promise.
-This is your plan? Hide out in a hotel?


01:01:11.734 --> 01:01:15.226
Doesn't look like they have
chicken tenders here, either.


01:01:31.688 --> 01:01:35.351
This is awesome.
Can we order room service?


01:01:35.458 --> 01:01:37.949
-Are you crazy? l'm going home.
-No.


01:01:38.528 --> 01:01:41.793
-The only place you're safe is with me.
-Safe with you?


01:01:41.898 --> 01:01:45.390
-Everybody's trying to kill you.
-l know. lsn't it cool?


01:01:45.601 --> 01:01:50.163
Hey, Bob, if you want to marry my mom,
l'll personally write the invitations.


01:02:19.635 --> 01:02:21.102
Love you, Bob.


01:02:35.852 --> 01:02:37.479
Be realistic, Bob.


01:02:42.625 --> 01:02:43.990
<i>-Hello.</i>
<i>-Hi, Gillian.</i>


01:02:44.093 --> 01:02:45.822
<i>Hi, sweetheart.</i>


01:02:45.928 --> 01:02:48.396
Yeah, Grandpa just fell asleep.
l was gonna call you guys.


01:02:49.265 --> 01:02:51.563
l have to tell you something.


01:02:51.667 --> 01:02:54.932
l know this is going to hurt you,
but l have to tell you.


01:02:55.037 --> 01:02:57.562
<i>-Are you all right?</i>
-l'm fine.


01:02:58.407 --> 01:03:00.932
-lt's about Bob.
<i>-What about him?</i>


01:03:01.043 --> 01:03:04.604
He's not who you think he is.
He's a spy, a Chinese spy.


01:03:04.714 --> 01:03:08.081
And these terrorists are trying to kill him,
and now the ClA's after him, too, and they.. .


01:03:08.184 --> 01:03:11.642
Farren, l know you don't like Bob,
but come on.


01:03:11.754 --> 01:03:14.279
<i>l'd expect this from lan, but not from you.</i>


01:03:14.390 --> 01:03:18.486
What? No, it's true. He's going
to get us all killed. Don't you even care?


01:03:18.861 --> 01:03:21.830
<i>Farren, this conversation is over.</i>
<i>Put Bob on.</i>


01:03:29.839 --> 01:03:30.965
Hi, Gillian.


01:03:31.073 --> 01:03:34.338
Bob, l am so sorry.
l don't know what's gotten into her.


01:03:36.479 --> 01:03:38.413
-lt's true.
<i>-What is?</i>


01:03:40.216 --> 01:03:42.377
Everything she said is all true.


01:03:42.919 --> 01:03:45.319
Whatever this is, it isn't funny.


01:03:45.621 --> 01:03:47.248
The kids are safe, l promise.


01:03:47.356 --> 01:03:50.189
l'll give them to you
as soon as you get back.


01:03:50.626 --> 01:03:54.756
You're either telling me the truth
or l've left my kids with a nut job.


01:03:56.766 --> 01:03:59.360
Either way, you should come and get them.


01:04:17.053 --> 01:04:21.547
So, you got any other cool spy stuff,
besides the watch?


01:04:28.464 --> 01:04:31.592
Don't touch. lt's very sharp.


01:04:32.468 --> 01:04:34.231
Cool. What else?


01:04:45.414 --> 01:04:46.438
Cool.


01:05:02.798 --> 01:05:04.265
Sorry, mister.


01:05:06.168 --> 01:05:07.760
Airport. Step on it.


01:05:29.258 --> 01:05:32.887
-Bob? Are you awake?
-Are you kidding?


01:05:34.730 --> 01:05:38.530
-Does he always snore like that?
-Can't you hear him next door?


01:05:38.901 --> 01:05:41.301
l always thought it was the pig.


01:05:44.640 --> 01:05:47.404
lt's over with you and Gillian, isn't it?


01:05:49.545 --> 01:05:51.410
Yes, Farren, it's over.


01:05:52.982 --> 01:05:56.748
-You win.
-Then why don't l feel like l won?


01:05:57.520 --> 01:06:01.047
lf you really loved her,
you wouldn't give up this easily.


01:06:01.958 --> 01:06:07.123
lt's because l love her and the three of you
that l have to walk away.


01:06:07.830 --> 01:06:10.424
lt's more important that you're safe.


01:06:12.134 --> 01:06:15.661
l thought l could put my other life
behind me, but l can't.


01:06:16.539 --> 01:06:20.168
Be glad.
You're lucky you're not joining this family.


01:06:22.912 --> 01:06:27.645
You've no idea what it's like to live in
a place where you totally don't belong.


01:06:27.750 --> 01:06:30.844
Don't be so sure. l was an orphan.


01:06:31.420 --> 01:06:36.255
l was raised in a group home.
l never knew my parents, but l had a family.


01:06:37.159 --> 01:06:40.185
l had dozens of brothers and sisters there.


01:06:40.596 --> 01:06:44.692
And l wasn't related to any of them,
but l loved them all.


01:06:47.336 --> 01:06:49.827
Family isn't whose blood you carry.


01:06:50.973 --> 01:06:53.840
lt's who you love and who loves you.


01:07:03.719 --> 01:07:05.186
-Gillian!
-Mom!


01:07:12.128 --> 01:07:16.030
Gillian, l'm really sorry about everything.


01:07:22.238 --> 01:07:25.867
Tell me the truth. Are you really a spy?


01:07:27.943 --> 01:07:32.175
Yes, l am. l was going to tell you at dinner,
but you stopped me.


01:07:33.282 --> 01:07:36.911
l don't care. You put my children in danger.


01:07:38.154 --> 01:07:39.348
Just go.


01:07:46.062 --> 01:07:49.896
Bob, when are we going to see you again?


01:07:52.368 --> 01:07:53.562
You're not.


01:08:03.879 --> 01:08:08.441
Please don't go away.
Who's gonna sing me China songs?


01:08:18.194 --> 01:08:22.028
-You'll be safe. l promise.
-Stay away from my children.


01:09:11.614 --> 01:09:15.414
<i>Dear Mom, l am very sorry,</i>
<i>but l cannot stay here.</i>


01:09:15.518 --> 01:09:18.715
<i>My destiny is to be a spy, like Bob.</i>


01:09:23.526 --> 01:09:28.554
<i>l am going with him.</i>
<i>Best wishes, your son, lan.</i>


01:10:11.140 --> 01:10:13.904
Ho's signal just popped back up.
We got him.


01:10:16.278 --> 01:10:17.643
Let's roll.


01:10:42.571 --> 01:10:45.438
Bob! Bob!


01:10:46.609 --> 01:10:48.600
-lan.
-You left your watch.


01:10:49.111 --> 01:10:51.272
What are you doing here? Let's go.


01:10:52.414 --> 01:10:54.882
What do you mean? We just got here.


01:11:05.294 --> 01:11:10.197
Bob Ho. What a coincidence. Tie them up.


01:11:17.673 --> 01:11:20.403
-What are you doing here, lan?
-l'm coming with you.


01:11:20.509 --> 01:11:21.942
l want to be a spy, too.


01:11:23.345 --> 01:11:26.803
ls this the bad guy?
l thought he'd be better dressed.


01:11:29.218 --> 01:11:32.244
-How did you find me?
-l found one of your tracking devices


01:11:32.354 --> 01:11:34.948
and put it in your pocket
when l hugged you goodbye.


01:11:35.057 --> 01:11:37.218
-l'm impressed.
-Thanks.


01:11:37.326 --> 01:11:40.853
-Can we go back to business?
-Would it help to mention l'm retired?


01:11:40.963 --> 01:11:43.227
Retired men don't download secrets.


01:11:43.332 --> 01:11:46.096
-l never downloaded anything.
-He's lying.


01:11:47.269 --> 01:11:50.329
Who are you going to believe?
Me or the traitor?


01:11:50.973 --> 01:11:54.306
Someone has been a very naughty boy.


01:11:55.244 --> 01:11:59.078
He's got cameras and microphones
mounted all over the place.


01:11:59.815 --> 01:12:02.340
Good plan, filming us together.


01:12:02.951 --> 01:12:06.114
-How could you turn against your country?
-lt's simple.


01:12:06.922 --> 01:12:08.685
l'm gonna be a billionaire.


01:12:08.791 --> 01:12:13.490
That file that you didn't download?
lt's a formula for a Growth Bacteria Hybrid.


01:12:13.595 --> 01:12:17.554
This stuff literally eats oil.
Can you imagine?


01:12:18.067 --> 01:12:21.935
Overnight,
all the world's oil supplies go poof.


01:12:22.037 --> 01:12:25.700
All except for Russia's.
lt'll be priceless, right, comrade?


01:12:26.542 --> 01:12:28.339
How did you get Colt to go along with you?


01:12:28.444 --> 01:12:31.174
Colt? That hillbilly's not part of this.


01:12:31.280 --> 01:12:32.941
He doesn't know what goes on
in the real world.


01:12:33.048 --> 01:12:35.016
He still thinks wrestling is real.


01:12:35.117 --> 01:12:37.847
Let the boy go.
He has nothing to do with this.


01:12:37.953 --> 01:12:41.548
Mr. Chit-Chat just laid out our whole plan.


01:12:45.661 --> 01:12:47.754
We cannot let him go.


01:12:48.230 --> 01:12:52.098
-He will tell.
-Trust me, no one would believe him.


01:12:52.701 --> 01:12:54.532
He's right about that.


01:12:56.805 --> 01:13:00.502
Hey, boss. Look at what l found
sneaking around outside.


01:13:01.477 --> 01:13:03.604
-Farren?
-Hi, everybody.


01:13:04.346 --> 01:13:06.337
Please, have a seat.


01:13:07.816 --> 01:13:09.306
This can't be happening.


01:13:10.586 --> 01:13:15.114
Poldark, let the children go
and l will find this GBH file for you.


01:13:15.491 --> 01:13:18.551
GBH? Like, Stockholm GBH?


01:13:19.194 --> 01:13:22.391
-How do you know that?
-No freaking way.


01:13:22.498 --> 01:13:25.467
You're telling me all of this is
because he downloaded a bootleg concert?


01:13:25.567 --> 01:13:27.034
You did what?


01:13:28.070 --> 01:13:29.970
You downloaded it?


01:13:30.072 --> 01:13:33.007
Wow, these companies take piracy
way too seriously.


01:13:33.108 --> 01:13:36.236
You were messing with my computer?
That's private.


01:13:36.345 --> 01:13:38.210
l just wanted to seem cool.


01:13:38.347 --> 01:13:41.009
You don't need to. You are cool.


01:13:41.417 --> 01:13:45.319
-You're one of the coolest kids l know.
-Really? Thanks.


01:13:45.421 --> 01:13:48.948
Hey, over here. Man with a gun.


01:13:49.258 --> 01:13:52.557
Wait a minute.
l am one of the only kids you know.


01:13:53.662 --> 01:13:57.223
-Where is the file?
-lt's on my iPod, on my desk at home.


01:13:58.267 --> 01:14:03.364
Now, see, you want to be a spy.
Never tell the truth to the bad guy.


01:14:03.806 --> 01:14:05.865
Sorry, l'm new at this.


01:14:06.341 --> 01:14:10.505
Tatiana, take some men to the kid's house
and find the iPod.


01:14:11.413 --> 01:14:13.472
What if the family is home?


01:14:15.284 --> 01:14:17.878
Ever since you dyed your hair blonde.. .
Kill them.


01:14:17.986 --> 01:14:21.547
-No, don't!
-Go, bring me that iPod.


01:14:21.990 --> 01:14:23.480
Come on, go. Go.


01:14:36.472 --> 01:14:38.667
Now, as for you.. .


01:15:11.940 --> 01:15:13.100
Awesome!


01:15:28.557 --> 01:15:30.149
Farren, let's go.


01:15:31.593 --> 01:15:35.222
-l call dibs on the front.
-Then l pick the radio station.


01:15:38.834 --> 01:15:40.199
Okay. Ready?


01:15:42.304 --> 01:15:43.771
Okay, hold on.


01:15:45.607 --> 01:15:47.768
-Hello?
-Gillian, listen to me.


